<!-- pushback -->
**What the ops director would push back on.** The unimpeded time is fixed on {{ v('policy.fit_years') }}, so a route that got slower for reasons no airline controls shows up here as padding that shrank. That is true, and it is the right direction for the error: with the reference fixed, growth in congestion cannot hide growth in padding. Recomputing the reference every year, the obvious alternative, drifts with congestion and hides exactly the growth this chapter measures; the first notebook keeps that dead end.

